  "description": "NIPLII crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C132 H98 Lu4 N2 O24,2(C7 H8). From the CIF bond table, Lu1 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu2 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu1A (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu2A (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu3 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu4 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu3A (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu4A (Lu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.556-3.734 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.28-109.49°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Lu4(μ3-OH)2(Ph2acac)8(o-O2NC6H4O)2]·2C7H8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
